sso_code.description:
**[Open this link to sign in]({authorize_url})**, on a computer.

Keycloak then sends you to an address starting with `enki://`, which no browser can open. That address holds the code, and the surest way to read it is to have the network panel open before you sign in:

1. press **F12**, open the **Network** tab, leave it open;
2. sign in;
3. the last line is the `enki://` address — right-click it and copy it.

Sometimes it is simply left in the address bar, in which case copy it from there. The code lasts about a minute, so paste it straight away; if it is refused, open the link again.
